1
00:00:00,825 --> 00:00:04,285
(Sheldon:)...he is with Wolowitz and Koothrappali
setting up her stereo.

2
00:00:04,996 --> 00:00:07,786
(Penny:)Oh, they're all up there, huh?
Hmm. Typical.

3
00:00:09,125 --> 00:00:11,125
(Sheldon:)It's axiomatically atypical.

4
00:00:12,295 --> 00:00:16,595
(Sheldon:)Until recently, they did not know Alicia, and
had no encounters in a previous location.

5
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:19,010
(Sheldon:)They never went
to visit the former tenants.

6
00:00:19,219 --> 00:00:23,639
So your characterization of their behavior
as typical is demonstrably fallacious.

7
00:00:26,309 --> 00:00:28,899
(Penny:)Okay, now I see the giant squid head.

8
00:00:31,982 --> 00:00:34,152
[DOOR OPENS THEN CLOSES]

9
00:00:36,027 --> 00:00:38,987
(Sheldon:)Oh, great.
Now I have to start all over again.

10
00:00:41,032 --> 00:00:43,162
(Howard:)Yeah, I thought about renting
this apartment...

11
00:00:43,368 --> 00:00:47,618
...but I'm really more of a downtown-loft
kind of guy.

12
00:00:47,831 --> 00:00:49,621
(Alicia:)Cool. So are you in a loft now?

13
00:00:49,833 --> 00:00:53,213
Oh, actually I'm living
with a woman in Altadena.

14
00:00:53,420 --> 00:00:56,210
Purely platonic. She's also my maid. Heh.

15
00:00:56,923 --> 00:01:02,023
- Sounds like a sweet deal.
- Well, I won't lie. It's pretty dope.

